00:00:22.866 --> 00:00:25.843
- Nowadays I find it
pretty easy to talk about

00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:27.120
my assault.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.120
I don't know if that's because
I've processed it so well

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.744
or I just really haven't
processed it very well at all

00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:35.827
and I just can't feel those emotions.

00:00:42.105 --> 00:00:44.031
- Two dudes grabbed me by the shoulders

00:00:44.031 --> 00:00:46.126
held me in place against a countertop

00:00:46.126 --> 00:00:49.511
while she, the older
woman, proceeded to just

00:00:49.511 --> 00:00:52.898
peel off my clothing and touch me wherever

00:00:52.898 --> 00:00:53.968
she felt like it.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:56.766
She groped me, she laughed at me.

00:00:56.766 --> 00:00:59.266
- He grabbed me, he groped me,

00:01:00.183 --> 00:01:03.655
he grabbed my crotch multiple times.

00:01:03.655 --> 00:01:05.600
I wasn't sure what was
happening, and he looked at me

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.560
and he said, "What's wrong?"

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.452
And I said, "Something
doesn't feel right."

00:01:10.452 --> 00:01:13.037
And he goes, "Nothing's
happening, nothing's wrong."

00:01:13.037 --> 00:01:15.748
- Things kept getting rougher and rougher.

00:01:15.748 --> 00:01:19.177
He grabbed me really
forcefully by the throat

00:01:19.177 --> 00:01:20.795
and I couldn't breathe.

00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:23.004
He hit me really hard across the face

00:01:23.004 --> 00:01:27.657
and he was huge and muscle-y
and holding me down.

00:01:27.657 --> 00:01:30.023
I just felt moisture coming down my face

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.722
and I was like, "Oh you're crying."

00:01:32.722 --> 00:01:34.707
- There's so many people who are survivors

00:01:34.707 --> 00:01:37.787
of some sort of rape or sexual assault

00:01:37.787 --> 00:01:41.047
so what we do is tend to
shut down survivor stories.

00:01:41.047 --> 00:01:44.635
- Hearing people's responses
to it made me feel like

00:01:44.635 --> 00:01:47.345
I couldn't trust my own intuition.

00:01:47.345 --> 00:01:50.532
- The most damaging thing I heard was

00:01:50.532 --> 00:01:53.767
"By talking about it, you're
giving him more power."

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:58.230
- He told me, "I'm sorry
you felt you were raped."

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:01.647
I felt not heard, I felt assaulted again.

00:02:11.609 --> 00:02:15.407
- A culture that we learn
to treat people like things

00:02:15.407 --> 00:02:18.022
and you don't treat people like things.

00:02:18.022 --> 00:02:20.286
- When I told my best
friend and she was silent,

00:02:20.286 --> 00:02:22.386
that was still a very clear, loud response

00:02:22.386 --> 00:02:24.045
that I was making her uncomfortable

00:02:24.045 --> 00:02:26.534
and I should stop talking.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:29.672
- Sexual violence is
prevalent at a massive level

00:02:29.672 --> 00:02:30.505
in this country.

00:02:30.505 --> 00:02:33.943
We tend to not believe
people because sometimes

00:02:33.943 --> 00:02:36.255
it's too much and then other times because

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:39.294
people have a vested interest
in not talking about rape

00:02:39.294 --> 00:02:41.430
and not talking about sexual violence.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:44.078
What ends up happening is
incredible damage to people,

00:02:44.078 --> 00:02:47.226
their sense of self, their
sense of trust in others.

00:02:47.226 --> 00:02:52.079
I want people, all genders,
always talking about consent,

00:02:52.079 --> 00:02:53.969
not taking it for granted that somebody

00:02:53.969 --> 00:02:56.373
wants to do something
because you hope that

00:02:56.373 --> 00:02:57.842
they want to do something.

00:02:57.842 --> 00:03:00.736
Reaching for empathy, the
sense of I'm worthwhile,

00:03:00.736 --> 00:03:04.132
I'm valuable and so I should
negotiate on my behalf.

00:03:04.132 --> 00:03:07.086
And people respecting
that you get to choose,

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.505
even if that disappoints
me, even if I don't like it,

00:03:10.505 --> 00:03:13.474
but that you still respect
somebody's sovereignty.

00:03:13.474 --> 00:03:16.095
Sexuality can be edgy
and it can be exciting

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.440
and it can have an intensity to it,

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.111
but that's not rape and
that's not violence,

00:03:21.111 --> 00:03:23.366
those are other things
that are not negotiated,

00:03:23.366 --> 00:03:25.029
that are not consensual.

00:03:25.029 --> 00:03:27.477
I want people to find
pleasure in their daily lives

00:03:27.477 --> 00:03:29.734
with one another and with themselves.

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:31.913
I believe pleasure and
connection are the antidote

00:03:31.913 --> 00:03:34.163
to trauma and rape culture.

